e numbers output by the run.\n```\n\nAlso save supplementary per-query-guide mapping (inverse table) as output/query_guide_assignments.csv? \"Never add extra rows to required artifacts\" — additional explanatory data may go into report.md or supplementary files. I'll put the full per-query-guide table in report.md (markdown table), plus a supplementary file output/supplementary_query_guide_assignments.csv. Hmm, keep it minimal: report.md table is enough. Actually a supplementary CSV is useful and allowed (\"belongs to report.md or supplementary files\"). Let me add output/supplementary_query_guide_mapping.csv. Hmm — optional; include it, it's cheap.\n\nSoftmax confidence: exp(c_i)/sum_j exp(c_j) across all 42 query guides for that gene. With correlations ~0.5-0.9, softmax may saturate (differences large). Fine.\n\nNow, the ambiguity quantification for the report:\n- margin = score − runner_up_score per gene\n- assignment stability under subsampling\n- identify genes with weakest margin\n- count of NT query guides correctly matching NT (10 NT query guides: correlation of each with NT signature vs best non-NT)\n- cross-dataset shift metrics: Pearson correlation between NT mean profiles; correlation of control mean profiles.\n\nAlso let me double-check \"cell type shift\": compute overall correlation between dataset NT mean profiles. Include in the report.\n\nEdge cases: Pearson correlation on signature vectors that include the target gene itself: e.g., PABPC1 KD signature includes negative PABPC1 expression — legitimate biology.\n\nPotential confound: query guides guide1..32 are anonymized, but are the guide sequences in var? No, var is empty. OK.\n\nOK writing analysis.py.\n\nFor Hungarian: scipy.optimize.linear_sum_assignment with cost = −C (rectangular 34×42 works; assigns each row a unique column).\n\nSorting: CSV rows sorted alphabetically by target_gene for determinism.\n\nRounding: keep full float precision (repr) — no problem for CSV.\n\nSubsample validation: for each guide group in each dataset, sample 50% of cells (seed=0), recompute everything, reassign, compare assigned query_guide_id per target_gene. Report stability rate. This is truly independent noise perturbation.\n\nAlso NT sanity: assert the assigned guide for NT row is an NT guide, and each NT query guide's best-correlating reference gene is NT (report fraction).\n\nTime to write the script. Watch out for dense memory: 4183×11858 float32 ≈ 198 MB; fine. Query: 3516×11858 ≈ 167 MB. float32 OK.\n\nGroup means: pandas groupby on numpy arrays: use np.add.reduceat after argsort, or scipy sparse groupby. Simplest: for each group, boolean mask indexing — 43 groups × sparse slice is fine. Or np.unique with return_inverse and np.bincount per gene — vectorized: labels→codes, then np.add.reduceat on dense sorted matrix. I'll do a small loop per group over sparse slices and take mean(axis=0) → np.asarray. 43+42 iterations, cheap.\n\nLet me write it."}}
